  "permanent_motion": "A continuous, subtle grain-shift filter applied to the 'background-texture.png'. All three main circles ('circle-etat-niger-border', 'circle-somair-border', 'circle-orano-border') should exhibit a gentle, slow 'breathing' pulse (slight scale up/down) throughout the entire duration of the scene, starting from their appearance.",

  "remotion_implementation_notes": "Use Remotion's <AbsoluteFill> for background. For textured circles, use <Img src={circle-paper-texture.png} /> positioned and sized, then apply a CSS clip-path property using the SVG path from the corresponding circle border. Text elements should use a custom font if available, otherwise a sans-serif font like 'Roboto' or 'Inter'. SVG paths can be animated using 'stroke-dashoffset' for 'draw-stroke' transitions. For 'stamp-impact', combine scale, rotation, and slight bounce. 'pulse' can be achieved with a small scale animation using 'spring()'. Ensure z-index values are respected for layering. Icons should be tinted using CSS 'filter: invert() sepia() saturate() hue-rotate() brightness() contrast()'.",

  "fidelity_warnings": "The exact 'aged paper' texture inside the circles and the background's subtle crumpling and fiber details might be hard to perfectly replicate with simple CSS or generic image generation. The hand-drawn, slightly imperfect quality of the 'DOSSIER' stamp border and the arrow/dotted line strokes (especially their ends) may require manual SVG path adjustments or a custom font for the stamp text to achieve the precise 'stamped' look. Shadows under elements are not explicitly defined but implied by the storyboard's depth; these would need to be added programmatically with CSS 'drop-shadow' or similar."
